-`sidebar_bg` optionally gives the desktop sidebar its own background. When omitted, the sidebar keeps the host terminal background. `active_row_bg` changes the active Space and focused Agent row background without affecting separators or scrollbar tracks. `selection_bg` changes the Navigate-mode cursor row background in the sidebar.
+`sidebar_bg` optionally gives the desktop sidebar its own background. When omitted, the sidebar keeps the host terminal background. `active_row_bg` changes the active Space and focused Agent row background without affecting separators or scrollbar tracks. `selection_bg` changes the Navigate-mode cursor row background in the sidebar. `pane_border` and `pane_border_focused` color the split-pane borders; they default to `overlay0` and `accent`, so muted text and the accent can differ from the borders.
 
 Color values accept hex, named colors, `rgb(r,g,b)`, or reset aliases like `reset`, `default`, `none`, and `transparent`.
 
